Question 01 — School Management System

A School Management System manages different types of employees in a school. Each employee has a name and salary, but there are specialized employees such as Teachers and Clerks that have unique duties.

Each Employee contains an IDCard that stores identification details, meaning IDCard is a part of Employee and cannot exist without it.

Additionally, the school has multiple Departments, and each Employee is associated with a Department. However, a Department can exist independently of a specific employee.

Different types of employees have unique implementations of the work() method, which need to be overridden in the respective classes.

a) Implement a class called Employee with name(String) and salary(double) attributes.
i. Create a method called work() that prints a generic message.

b) Create two classes called Teacher and Clerk as subclasses of Employee.
i. Override the work() method to display unique messages for each type.

c) Implement an IDCard class with cardNumber(String) as an attribute.
i. The IDCard should be part of an Employee using Composition and initialized within the Employee constructor.

d) Create a class called Department with departmentName(String) and location(String) attributes.
i. A Department should be associated with an Employee using Aggregation.

e) Modify the Teacher and Clerk classes to include a Department for each class.

f) Create a SchoolApp class with a main method to:
i. Create objects for Teacher and Clerk with their IDCards.
ii. Assign Departments to those employees.
iii. Call the work() method and display full details.

